    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0424" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg412"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20 Missions/17</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-23">June 23,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Chief of the U.S.
                    Military Mission to Iran, General Ridley, has submitted a report on his Mission
                    and has recommended that the Mission be recalled. A copy of this report and
                    recommendation are attached hereto.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d424-f1"/> The War
                    Department agrees with General Ridley that there exists no military necessity
                    for this Mission and that virtually its entire usefulness to Iran has already
                    been accomplished. It is felt that the Mission should be withdrawn <pb
                        facs="0425" n="413" xml:id="pg413"/> whether or not the Iranian Government
                    agrees. However, the Military Mission to Iran originally was dispatched because
                    of State Department considerations and no action leading to its withdrawal will
                    be taken without your agreement. Will you kindly inform the War Department of
                    your views on this matter.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
